    "description": "Are you interested in helping support, promote, and grow competitive\nbicycle racing in Iowa?\n\nWant to help shape the racing scene?\n\nThen consider running to become a board member of the Iowa Bicycle\nRacing Association (IBRA). IBRA will be electing it's board members\nduring the January 24th board meeting in Des Moines. Up to 8 officers\nwill be elected (electronically ahead of time, or onsite at the meeting).\n\nRequirements:\n- Nominees must be a member in good standing of an Iowa-based,\nUSAC-sanctioned club.\n- No single club may have more than one board member elected.\n\nResponsibilities:\n- Assist other board members in supporting, promoting, and growing\nbicycle racing in Iowa.\n- Participate in monthly board conference call/meetings.\n- Physically attend board meetings (typically in January)\n\nIf you, or a club member you know, is interested in running for the IBRA\nboard, please contact Jeff Mertz off-list.\n\nNominations are due by Friday, January 16th at 12:00 pm.\n\nBallots and voting will begin on Friday, January 16th and end at 10:30\nam on Saturday, January 24th (at the beginning of the IBRA board meeting).",
